# Leave VITE_API_URL unset to run fully on the built-in mock data (seed JSON).
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Sign-in. Leave VITE_PRIVY_APP_ID unset and the site runs read-only: no sign-in
# in the nav, a one-line note instead of actions that need an account, and no
# Privy SDK in the bundle at all. A dev build with it unset signs in as the
# demo wallet instead (src/lib/devWallet.ts), which never reaches a production
# build. Set it to Sera.cx's existing Privy app id (the one g.sera.cx and
# sera-pay use) for real sign-in; causes.sera.cx and http://localhost:3100 have
# to be in that app's allowed origins.
# VITE_PRIVY_APP_ID=

# Optional, local development only. The demo signer in src/lib/devWallet.ts
# derives its account from Ganache's public default mnemonic, so no private key
# is committed anywhere in this repository. Set this only if you would rather
# sign local writes as some other test account. It MUST NEVER be a key that
# holds funds on any network, and it is never read in a production build: the
# module it belongs to is aliased away and cannot be bundled.
# VITE_DEV_PRIVATE_KEY=

# EIP-712 domain. Must match the API's CHAIN_ID and REGISTRY_ADDRESS.
# VITE_CHAIN_ID=11155111
# VITE_REGISTRY_ADDRESS=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
